//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: `str` has no `-`; it is defined only on `i64` and `f64`
//@ error-contains: `bool` has no `+`; it is defined only on `i64`, `f64` and `str`
//@ error-contains: has no `*`; it is defined only on `i64` and `f64`
//@ error-contains: `bool` has no `bnot`; it is defined only on `i64`
//
// Each operator is defined on a fixed domain — `+` on `i64`, `f64` and `str`
// (concatenation), the rest of the arithmetic on `i64` and `f64`, the bitwise
// family and `bnot` on `i64` — because that is exactly what codegen emits.
// Sharing a type is not enough: every line below pairs two operands of one
// type, and every line is wrong.
//
// This file exists because the checker once stopped at "the operands share a
// type": `"a" - "b"` and `[1] * [2]` sailed through to the C compiler, where
// the error surfaced as `neon_i64_sub` on structs, and `true + false` COMPILED
// AND RAN as C integer addition on a bool.

fn main() {
    let s = "a" - "b";
    let b = true + false;
    let l = [1] * [2];
    let n = bnot true;
}
